  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider the following statements:<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>: Rishi is a judge.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>: Rishi is honest.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>: Rishi is not arrogant.</p><p>The negation of the statement &quot;if Rishi is a judge and he is not arrogant, then he is honest&quot; is</p>"
  },
